From: baseband lane
Subject: 0518 pandora_pas: put the PIL metadata behind an SHM bridge, as qcom_tzmem does

Everything else has been ruled out by hardware evidence from 2026-11-21:

  * nine PAS ids, including pas 0, all gave a0 0xffcfffbb for the same metadata blob;
  * shm_bridge_enable returns a0 0 and the next INIT_IMAGE still gives 0xffcfffbb;
  * the metadata blob's construction was checked field by field against qcom_mdt_read_metadata().

Upstream's qcom_tzmem.c wraps that metadata in an SHM bridge, and only uses the plain path when the
bridge is unsupported:

    pfn_and_ns_perm = paddr | QCOM_SCM_PERM_RW;          // 0x6
    ipfn_and_s_perm = paddr | QCOM_SCM_PERM_RW;
    size_and_flags  = size | (1 << QCOM_SHM_BRIDGE_NUM_VM_SHIFT);   // 9
    qcom_scm_shm_bridge_create(pfn_and_ns_perm, ipfn_and_s_perm, size_and_flags,
                               QCOM_SCM_VMID_HLOS, &handle);        // svc 0xc, cmd 0x1e

with the handle in a1 and a delete (svc 0xc, cmd 0x1d) once AUTH_AND_RESET has been made.  This adds
exactly that: the bridge is created before INIT_IMAGE, its handle lives with the metadata slot, and
it is deleted by pas_meta_release() after auth or shutdown.

